Bob is the companion of Old Man Scrazzy, a head without a body beneath a long cloak that drapes from the neck down. He floats where Scrazzy needs him, and no one has seen a foot under the hem. He is young and talkative, hums while he works, and asks to be called Bob. He sees in the dark and serves as the old man's eyes, and he works magic, throwing lightning out of his head hard enough to blow his cloak back.
